# Benchmark artifacts #
#######################
# Models, their configurations and the string vocabulary are written together by
# scripts/generate_benchmark_models.py. A model is ~190 MB, so the whole directory
# is generated on demand rather than committed. See documentation/benchmarking.md.
benchmark-data/generated/

# Bundles from scripts/benchmark/package.sh -- a build artifact of the working tree.
benchmark-data/dist/

# The Triton comparison harness: model repository generator, server runner, gRPC load
# generator and the arm results it collects. Kept beside the code so a campaign can be
# re-run without hunting for it, but deliberately untracked -- it is scaffolding for
# measuring somebody else's server, not part of hushar. The findings it produced are in
triton-bench/

# Runbooks and working notes for our own benchmark campaigns. These name accounts,
# regions, bucket names and instance types we happen to be using, which is operational
# detail rather than anything a reader of this repository needs. The reusable parts of a
# campaign belong in documentation/ and benchmark-data/results/ instead.
benchmark-data/private/

# The config sweeps from the first round of benchmarking, retired here when a narrower
# round started. 69 MB and 6,539 files of breadth -- every threading permutation on every
# accelerator -- which is more evidence than insight for someone reading the repository,
# and it is superseded the moment the service's own numbers move. Kept on disk so the old
# figures can still be looked up, untracked so the repository carries only the round it is
# actually making a case with. See documentation/benchmarking.md §6.
benchmark-data/old-results/

# Written by scripts/benchmark/bootstrap.sh on a benchmark instance: that host's
# ORT_DYLIB_PATH and provider, which are per-host and not the repository's business.
/env.sh

# The write-up of the benchmark campaigns as a paper (LaTeX sources, generated figures and
# tables). It is a document about the results, not part of hushar, and is kept beside the
# repository rather than in it.
tabular-inference-paper/

# Rust build output #
#####################
/target/
*.profraw
*.profdata

# Python, for scripts/ #
########################
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# Environment files, potentially sensitive #
###########################################
.env
.env.*

# OS-specific files #
#####################

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Windows
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Editors and IDEs #
####################

# Visual Studio Code
.vscode/

# IntelliJ Rust / CLion
.idea/
*.iml

# Vim
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
.*.swp

# Emacs
*#*#
.#*

# Logs, temporary and backup files #
####################################
*.log

# ... except a benchmark's own logs under results/raw/. Those are the server banners, the
# per-second CPU samples and the client output a report's figures are traced to, so they are
# tracked on purpose -- see documentation/benchmarking.md §6.
!benchmark-data/results/**/raw/**/*.log

*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*~

# AI agents #
#############
.kiro/specs/*
!.kiro/specs/.gitkeep
.kiro/logs/*.log
.kiro/settings/lsp.json
*.kiro/steering
*.kiro/steering/*
.ai/
.agent/
.agents/
.gitagent/
.ottoai/
.cursor/
.cursor_mcp.json
.windsurf/
.windsurf/hooks.json
.aider*
.devin/
.autogpt/

# =========================================================================
# What to KEEP
# =========================================================================
!AGENTS.md
!CLAUDE.md
!SOUL.md
!RULES.md

# The account ids check_privacy.py should treat as known leaks, one per line. Untracked on
# purpose: an id committed to teach a scanner about it has still been committed. Supply it
# here or in $HUSHAR_ACCOUNT_IDS.
.account-ids

# Triton's raw Prometheus dumps stay in S3 only: they are verbatim counter text whose
# twelve-digit microsecond totals are indistinguishable from an AWS account id to any
# scanner, and every number derived from them is already in cells/. The `**` before the
# filename matters: the dumps sit one level down, under raw/server/<host>/.
benchmark-data/results/**/raw/server/**/*.metrics-*.txt
